<%# locals: () %>
<%# Notices and alerts as toasts in the bottom right (rune_ui's flash, toast: true), in a frame so a
    turbo stream can replace them. data-turbo-temporary keeps them out of Turbo's page cache, so a
    preview of a page never shows its toast again. The wrapper is there only with a message, and
    lays out as nothing (display: contents): a box here is an item in <main>'s column, whose gap
    would push the page down, and Turbo's cached preview (which drops it) would then jump. %>
<%= turbo_frame_tag :flash do %>
  <% if flash[:notice].present? || flash[:alert].present? %>
    <div class="flash-frame__messages" data-turbo-temporary>
      <%= flash_messages(toast: true) %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
